From 5a678178b7d70943067f1c043ea1103a06bd9f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(courses): secure course management module (backend, CMS,
 app)

Backend
- Admin course CRUD under /api/admin/courses: create, partial edit,
  publish/unpublish toggle, delete (blocked when students are enrolled)
- Category management under /api/admin/categories; public /api/categories
- Public catalog only returns published courses and never selects
  protected columns (vimeoId, pdfUrl)
- Firebase ID token auth; admin rights from the `admin` custom claim,
  plus tools/set-admin.mjs to grant/revoke it
- zod validation, central error handler (no internal error leaks),
  security headers, CORS allow-list, per-IP rate limiting
- Uploads: admin only, type checked by magic bytes, random file names
- Content: purchase check uses the verified token (removes the
  ?admin=true / ?uid= bypass); writes are admin only; folder delete
  is recursive; banners writes and stats now admin only

DB
- categories table; courses gain category_id, original_price,
  is_published, published_at, created_at, updated_at
- Idempotent migration that backfills categories and keeps existing
  courses published

CMS
- Authenticated API client; Course Manager (list/filter, edit, publish
  toggle, delete, MRP, thumbnail preview) and Categories tab
- Admin gate uses the custom claim instead of a hard-coded email list

App
- Categories and catalog from the API, correct paise -> rupee display,
  real MRP, content fetched with the user's ID token

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
