@@ -40,3 +40,47 @@ This will start the Expo bundler. Press `w` to open it in a web browser, or use
 
 ## Note
 Make sure the backend is always running before you test the mobile app or the CMS, otherwise the data will not load.
+
+## Course Management Module
+
+Admins manage courses and categories from the CMS (**Course Manager** and **Categories** tabs).
+The mobile app only ever sees **published** courses.
+
+### One-time setup
+1. **Database** – run the migration (safe to re-run):
+   ```
+   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f shared/db/migrations/0001_course_module.sql
+   ```
+   It adds the `categories` table, publish/pricing columns on `courses`, creates categories from the
+   existing course `category` values, and marks existing courses as published.
+2. **Make someone a CMS admin** – admin rights are a Firebase custom claim, checked by the backend on
+   every admin request (the old email allow-list in the CMS was only a UI check and is gone):
+   ```
+   cd Backend
+   node tools/set-admin.mjs grant admin@example.com   # also: revoke <email>, list
+   ```
+   The admin must log out of the CMS and log in again afterwards.
+3. **Environment** – see `.env.example` for the backend variables (`CORS_ORIGINS`, `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, ...)
+   and `VITE_API_URL` for the CMS.
+
+### API
+Public (mobile app):
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/api/courses?category=<slug>` | Published courses only |
+| GET | `/api/courses/:id` | 404 for drafts |
+| GET | `/api/categories` | |
+| GET | `/api/content/:courseId` | Firebase ID token required; must have purchased the course |
+
+Admin (Firebase ID token with `admin` claim, `Authorization: Bearer <token>`):
+| Method | Path | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| GET | `/api/admin/courses?status=all\|published\|draft&categoryId=&q=` | Includes drafts and enrollment counts |
+| GET | `/api/admin/courses/:id` | |
+| POST | `/api/admin/courses` | `{ title, description, price, originalPrice?, thumbnail, categoryId, isPublished? }` – prices in paise |
+| PATCH | `/api/admin/courses/:id` | Any subset of the fields above |
+| PATCH | `/api/admin/courses/:id/publish` | `{ isPublished }` |
+| DELETE | `/api/admin/courses/:id` | 409 if students are enrolled – unpublish instead |
+| GET/POST | `/api/admin/categories` | `{ name, slug?, sortOrder? }` |
+| PATCH/DELETE | `/api/admin/categories/:id` | Delete is 409 while courses use it |
+| POST | `/api/upload` | Multipart field `image`; PNG/JPEG/WEBP/PDF ≤ 500 KB, type checked by file content |
